repository-code: 'https://github.com/rajsubediresearch/GrowthFit.jl'
abstract: >-
  A Julia toolbox for fitting seven nested phenomenological growth models
  (Exponential Growth, Generalized Growth, Logistic, Generalized Logistic,
  Richards, Generalized Richards, and Gompertz) to epidemic incidence data
  by maximum likelihood under normal, Poisson, or negative-binomial (NB1)
  error structures. Provides parametric-bootstrap uncertainty
  quantification, short-term forecasting with prediction intervals,
  performance metrics including MAE, MSE, 95% prediction-interval coverage
  and the weighted interval score, and a local practical-identifiability
  screen based on parameter collinearity. A Julia port of the corresponding
  R and MATLAB toolboxes.
keywords:
  - epidemic forecasting
  - infectious disease modeling
  - phenomenological growth models
  - parameter estimation
  - uncertainty quantification
  - practical identifiability
  - Julia
